<%# One footer column, from the operator's navigation rows.

  A link whose target does not resolve -- an unpublished page, a deleted one -- is dropped by
  `marketing_nav` rather than rendered as a dead anchor. That is the mechanism behind the rule this rebuild
  started from: the old footer advertised four legal documents and a live chat and delivered four empty
  anchors.

  AN EXTERNAL LINK NOW SAYS SO, AND SAYS IT THROUGH THE ANCHOR'S OWN OPTIONS. The four links to the
  operator's published legal documents opened a new tab with nothing to announce it, and `target` and `rel`
  were spliced in as an `html_safe` literal -- a string that bypasses escaping in the one place an operator's
  data meets markup. They are tag options now, so `nil` simply omits the attribute, and the suffix is
  `sr-only` because the new tab is only news to someone who cannot see it happen.
%>
<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-lyn-ink-soft">
  <% marketing_nav(placement).each do |item| %>
    <li>
      <%= link_to item[:href],
                  class: 'rounded-lg hover:text-lyn-ink focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-lyn-blue',
                  target: ('_blank' if item[:external]),
                  rel: ('noopener' if item[:external]) do %>
        <%= item[:label] %>
        <% if item[:external] %>
          <span class="sr-only"><%= t('marketing.footer.opens_new_tab') %></span>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </li>
  <% end %>
</ul>
